      "statement": "Real git formats are used (rather than a custom encoding) so gadget code can be exported/imported to real repos later; only isomorphic-git's plumbing runs against a gitdir containing nothing but objects/**, with a virtual fs shim rejecting everything else so porcelain commands like git.commit/git.merge are unusable by construction.",
