    {
      "id": "claim_f398c1c4957b4ec18eb492777c469f7e",
      "statement": "Live pre-git chats are converted in place: the legacy doc is flattened once and the chat's uncommitted state becomes one synthetic \"changes\" message carrying a pin per touched permanent gadget; the boundary message is written even when nothing needs converting because ChatCodeBase.epoch points at it and replay keys pre-conversion read elision on it, with retired Yjs update bytes kept on disk as rollback insurance.",
